Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 06:18:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 059/119] scene-referred S0: r_SceneReferred master switch

First item of Stage S0 (SceneReferredSpec.md section 6). Adds the one piece of state that
tells the renderer to take the scene-referred path, with nothing behind it yet: the switch
is wired, read and documented, and no pass, format or constant changes as a result.

Decision: scene-notes/decisions/s0-master-switch.md, approach A (Pattern A + Pattern B kept
separate). Research: scene-notes/research/s0-cvar-gating-pattern.md.

- r_SceneReferred (RendererCVars, VF_NULL, default 1) is the user's kill switch, shaped after
  the r_DepthOfFieldLensModel block: it is never written by code, only honours or refuses a
  request, and its help string names the spec and states the byte-identity promise. VF_NULL
  and not VF_DUMPTODISK, like every other ccam cvar, so no forced value can ever be baked
  into a user config.
- The request itself is a per-frame parameter on the post-effect bus,
  Global_User_SceneReferred, registered at manager level next to the other Global_User_*
  params. The bLensModel precedent, for the same reasons: the bus already carries ccam's
  single-writer, handover and editor<->game semantics, and EF_ResetPostEffects() clears the
  request by itself, which is the correct behaviour for per-frame, per-camera state. A cvar
  written by ccam would have been dropped by ClearSavedBaselines() on entering game mode and
  stranded the engine off the stock path.
- CRendererResources::IsSceneReferred() = request && cvar. The later S0 items (fp16 forcing,
  exposure-path branch) and every later stage key on this and on nothing else.
- ccam gains a "Scene Referred" property group (Schematyc member name SceneReferred, default
  false while the pipeline is built stage by stage) plus ApplySceneReferred() /
  RestoreSceneReferred(). Applied editor-live from ENTITY_EVENT_UPDATE and on property
  change, under CanDriveRenderState(), latched and restored like every other ccam state, and
  added to RestoreAllEffects() and ClearSavedBaselines().
- docs/ConsoleReference.md gains the cvar under Live tuning; README.md gains the property
  group.

Built clean (0 errors, 0 warnings outside Code/SDKs): CryRenderD3D11, CinematicCamera.

